close_reason: "Bounded recent-activity reads shipped with derived per-stream bounds, a newest-rows context path, fallback receipts and a CI-gated benchmark"
contract_change:
  api: "runActivity, readRecentActivity, runContext (@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk, @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/query)"
  before: "ActivityResult and ContextResult had no read-cost disclosure, and the context activity section was built by a full runActivity page over every history stream"
  after: "ActivityResult gains an optional history_read receipt and ContextResult an optional activity_history_read receipt ({ reason, streams_read, streams_total }), present only when a read on a tracker with 500 or more history streams could not be bounded by its window; readRecentActivity({ limit }, global), ActivityHistoryReadReceipt and RecentActivityResult are new exports of @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/query; rows, totals, cursors and errors are unchanged"
  migrate: "No change for existing reads. Consumers that reject unknown result keys should allow the optional history_read and activity_history_read receipts; a consumer that needs only the newest rows can call readRecentActivity instead of runActivity with raw: true"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_added
  owner: pm-gh1664
  gate_id: history-read-costs
  negative_control: "node scripts/bench/history-read-costs.mjs --check removes runtime/history-stream-summary.json before every full-scan sample, forcing the complete read; that path measured p50 2,282-3,211 ms against a bounded p50 of 721-1,045 ms, so it fails both the 0.6-of-full-scan fraction gate and the enforced 1,542 ms ceiling, and tests/unit/commands/history/activity-bounded-reads.spec.ts counts the streams a warm digest parses"
  local_checks[3]: node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage,node scripts/bench/history-read-costs.mjs --check,node scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs --check
  hosted_checks[2]: CI / Gates (static),CI / Gates (coverage)
body: ""
